phux keeps only the fatal-signal terminal restore from the upstream crate and
does not track upstream verbatim (see ADR-0079). The local modifications,
including everything removed, are enumerated in the header comment of this
crate's Cargo.toml, as required by section 4(b) of the Apache License ("You
must cause any modified files to carry prominent notices stating that You
changed the files"). Each modified source file also carries a
`MODIFIED FROM UPSTREAM` banner naming the change.

The phux workspace is Apache-2.0. This crate keeps its own LICENSE and
NOTICE so the upstream grant and the local modifications stay visible on
exactly the derived files.

Modifications by the phux project are contributed under the same Apache-2.0
terms so the crate stays licensed as a single coherent unit.
